6:26:17 PM [express] GET /api/lessons/c3151c6b-b3ba-43a3-b066-b0535adb5415/exercises 200 in 7ms :: [{"id":"0b969664-ba90-4f23-9196-e0efcc7dde99","lessonId":"c3151c6b-b3ba-43a3-b066-b0535adb5415","type":"multiple_choice","difficulty":1,"question":"Arabic letters change shape based on their position in a word. How many forms does each letter have?","questionAr":"الحروف العربية تتغير حسب موقعها في الكلمة. كم شكلاً لكل حرف؟","context":"Unlike English where 'a' always looks the same, Arabic letters like ب can look like بـ ـبـ ـب depending on where they appear in a word.","contextAr":"على عكس الإنجليزية، الحروف العربية مثل ب تتغير شكلها حسب موقعها في الكلمة","hint":"Think about it: isolated, start of word, middle of word, end of word","hintAr":null,"options":["2 forms","3 forms","4 forms","5 forms"],"correctAnswer":"4 forms","explanation":"Each Arabic letter has 4 forms: isolated (ب), initial (بـ), medial (ـبـ), and final (ـب). This is because Arabic is written in connected script.","explanationAr":"لكل حرف ٤ أشكال: منفرد (ب)، بداية (بـ)، وسط (ـبـ)، نهاية (ـب)","grammarNote":"Some letters like أ (Alif), د (Dal), ذ (Dhal), ر (Ra), ز (Zay), و (Waw) only connect from the right side, so they only have 2 distinct forms.","grammarNoteAr":"بعض الحروف مثل أ، د، ذ، ر، ز، و تتصل من اليمين فقط، لذا لها شكلان فقط","skillType":"reading","xpReward":10,"orderIndex":1},{"id":"d7010924-b932-4929-967d-abace36c111f","lessonId":"c3151c6b-b3ba-43a3-b066-b0535adb5415","type":"multiple_choice","difficulty":1,"question":"Which letter is this: ب","questionAr":"ما هذا الحرف: ب","context":"ب (Ba) is the second letter of the Arabic alphabet. It sounds like the English 'b' in 'book'.\n\nVocabulary: ب is for بَاب (baab) = door, بِنْت (bint) = girl, بَيْت (bayt) = house","contextAr":"ب (الباء) هي الحرف الثاني في الأبجدية العربية. تشبه 'b' في الإنجليزية.\n\nمفردات: ب = باب، بنت، بيت","hint":null,"hintAr":null,"options":["Ta (ت)","Ba (ب)","Tha (ث)","Alif (ا)"],"correctAnswer":"Ba (ب)","explanation":"This is ب (Ba). It has ONE dot below. Compare: ت (Ta) has TWO dots above, ث (Tha) has THREE dots above.","explanationAr":"هذا ب (الباء). لها نقطة واحدة تحتها. قارن: ت (نقطتان فوق)، ث (ثلاث نقاط فوق)","grammarNote":null,"grammarNoteAr":null,"skillType":"reading","xpReward":10,"orderIndex":2},{"id":"088aa20e-5879-4fc6-b596-57cce0d05e5f","lessonId":"c3151c6b-b3ba-43a3-b066-b0535adb5415","type":"multiple_choice","difficulty":1,"question":"The word بَاب means 'door'. What sound does the first letter ب make?","questionAr":"كلمة بَاب تعني 'door'. ما صوت الحرف الأول ب؟","context":"New vocabulary:\n• بَاب (baab) = door\n• بِنْت (bint) = girl\n• بَيْت (bayt) = house\n\nAll three words start with ب (Ba), which sounds like English 'b'.","contextAr":"مفردات جديدة:\n• بَاب = door\n• بِنْت = girl\n• بَيْت = house","hint":null,"hintAr":null,"options":["Like 'p' in 'pen'","Like 'b' in 'book'","Like 'f' in 'fun'","Like 'm' in 'map'"],"correctAnswer":"Like 'b' in 'book'","explanation":"ب (Ba) sounds like 'b' in 'book'. Remember: بَاب (door), بِنْت (girl), بَيْت (house) — all start with the 'b' sound.","explanationAr":"ب تنطق مثل 'b' في الإنجليزية. تذكر: باب، بنت، بيت — كلها تبدأ بصوت 'ب'","grammarNote":null,"grammarNoteAr":null,"skillType":"reading","xpReward":10,"orderIndex":3},{"id":"529e88b1-752f-4169-bcb7-e078181614c3","lessonId":"c3151c6b-b3ba-43a3-b066-b0535adb5415","type":"multiple_choice","difficulty":1,"question":"How many dots does ت (Ta) have, and where are they?","questionAr":"كم نقطة لـ ت (التاء)، وأين هي؟","context":"New vocabulary:\n• تَمْر (tamr) = dates (the fruit)\n• ثَلْج (thalj) = snow\n\nThe letters ب، ت، ث all have the same base shape — only the dots differ! This is the key to telling them apart.","contextAr":"مفردات جديدة:\n• تَمْر = dates\n• ثَلْج = snow\n\nالحروف ب، ت، ث لها نفس الشكل الأساسي — فقط النقاط تختلف!","hint":null,"hintAr":null,"options":["1 dot below","2 dots above","3 dots above","No dots"],"correctAnswer":"2 dots above","explanation":"ت (Ta) has 2 dots ABOVE. Remember the pattern: ب (1 dot below) → ت (2 dots above) → ث (3 dots above). Dots are the key!","explanationAr":"ت لها نقطتان فوق. تذكر: ب (نقطة تحت) → ت (نقطتان فوق) → ث (ثلاث نقاط فوق)","grammarNote":null,"grammarNoteAr":null,"skillType":"reading","xpReward":10,"orderIndex":4},{"id":"e80a65e0-9647-450f-8fc4-282ae8cb5263","lessonId":"c3151c6b-b3ba-43a3-b066-b0535adb5415","type":"multiple_choice","difficulty":1,"question":"Look at the word بِنْت (bint = girl). Which letters do you recognize?","questionAr":"انظر لكلمة بِنْت (girl). أي حروف تعرفها؟","context":"بِنْت (bint) = girl. This word uses:\n• ب (Ba) — 1 dot below\n• ن (Nun) — like a bowl with 1 dot above\n• ت (Ta) — 2 dots above\n\nYou already know ب and ت from this lesson!","contextAr":"بِنْت = girl. الكلمة تستخدم: ب (نقطة تحت)، ن (مثل وعاء مع نقطة فوق)، ت (نقطتان فوق)","hint":null,"hintAr":null,"options":["Only ب","Only ت","Both ب and ت","Neither ب nor ت"],"correctAnswer":"Both ب and ت","explanation":"بِنْت starts with ب (Ba) and ends with ت (Ta). You know both! The middle letter ن (Nun) sounds like 'n' in 'nun'.","explanationAr":"بِنْت تبدأ بـ ب وتنتهي بـ ت. تعرفهما! الحرف الأوسط ن (النون) ينطق مثل 'n'","grammarNote":null,"grammarNoteAr":null,"skillType":"reading","xpReward":10,"orderIndex":5},{"id":"1bd0e21a-1c97-470a-9db0-52858f7100b7","lessonId":"c3151c6b-b3ba-43a3-b066-b0535adb5415","type":"fill_blank","difficulty":1,"question":"ب has 1 dot, ت has 2 dots. How many dots does ث have? ___","questionAr":"ب لها نقطة واحدة، ت لها نقطتان. كم نقطة لـ ث؟ ___","context":"ث (Tha) sounds like 'th' in 'think'. It appears in: ثَلْج (thalj) = snow, ثَمَر (thamar) = fruit.\n\nPattern: ب (1) → ت (2) → ث (?)","contextAr":"ث (الثاء) تنطق مثل 'th' في 'think'. تظهر في: ثَلْج = snow، ثَمَر = fruit","hint":"Follow the pattern: 1, 2, ___","hintAr":"اتبع النمط: ١، ٢، ___","options":null,"correctAnswer":"3","explanation":"ث has 3 dots above. The pattern: ب (1 dot below), ت (2 dots above), ث (3 dots above). Same shape, different dots!","explanationAr":"ث لها ثلاث نقاط فوق. النمط: ب (١)، ت (٢)، ث (٣). نفس الشكل، نقاط مختلفة!","grammarNote":null,"grammarNoteAr":null,"skillType":"reading","xpReward":15,"orderIndex":6},{"id":"03f0f13a-29f3-44ee-9600-1102a86ee1f8","lessonId":"c3151c6b-b3ba-43a3-b066-b0535adb5415","type":"multiple_choice","difficulty":1,"question":"أ (Alif) is the first letter of the Arabic alphabet. Which English vowel sound does it represent?","questionAr":"أ (الألف) هو أول حرف في الأبجدية. أي صوت في الإنجليزية يمثل؟","context":"أ (Alif) makes an 'a' or 'ah' sound. It's special: Alif is one of the non-connecting letters — it only connects to the letter before it, not after.\n\nNew words with Alif:\n• أَب (ab) = father\n• أُم (umm) = mother","contextAr":"أ (الألف) ينطق 'آ'. هو حرف غير متصل — يتصل بما قبله فقط.\n\nكلمات بالألف:\n• أَب = father\n• أُم = mother","hint":null,"hintAr":null,"options":["Like 'b' in 'book'","Like 'a' in 'father'","Like 'th' in 'think'","Like 't' in 'top'"],"correctAnswer":"Like 'a' in 'father'","explanation":"أ (Alif) makes the 'a' sound as in 'father'. It's the first letter of the Arabic alphabet and one of the most important!","explanationAr":"أ (الألف) ينطق مثل 'آ'. هو أول حرف في الأبجدية وأحد أهم الحروف","grammarNote":null,"grammarNoteAr":null,"skillType":"reading","xpReward":10,"orderIndex":7},{"id":"f428ec4e-8c69-4d2f-8197-1ee5cd864a67","lessonId":"c3151c6b-b3ba-43a3-b066-b0535adb5415","type":"sentence_order","difficulty":1,"question":"Arrange these letters by number of dots: least dots first → most dots last","questionAr":"رتّب هذه الحروف حسب عدد النقاط: الأقل أولاً","context":"You learned: ب (1 dot below), ت (2 dots above), ث (3 dots above), أ (no dots).","contextAr":"تعلمت: أ (بلا نقاط)، ب (١ نقطة)، ت (٢ نقاط)، ث (٣ نقاط)","hint":null,"hintAr":null,"options":["ث (3 dots)","ب (1 dot)","أ (no dots)","ت (2 dots)"],"correctAnswer":"أ (no dots) ب (1 dot) ت (2 dots) ث (3 dots)","explanation":"أ (0 dots) → ب (1 dot below) → ت (2 dots above) → ث (3 dots above). The dot pattern is the key to telling these letters apart!","explanationAr":"أ (٠) → ب (١) → ت (٢) → ث (٣). نمط النقاط هو المفتاح للتمييز بين الحروف!","grammarNote":null,"grammarNoteAr":null,"skillType":"reading","xpReward":15,"orderIndex":8},{"id":"eabaa6dd-1589-460d-8f0d-1d700e3df079","lessonId":"c3151c6b-b3ba-43a3-b066-b0535adb5415","type":"multiple_choice","difficulty":1,"question":"When ب appears in the MIDDLE of a word (medial position), what does it look like?","questionAr":"عندما تظهر ب في وسط الكلمة (الموضع الأوسط)، كيف تبدو؟","context":"Arabic letters connect like cursive writing. ب changes shape in each position:\n• Isolated: ب\n• Initial (start): بـ\n• Medial (middle): ـبـ\n• Final (end): ـب","contextAr":"الحروف العربية تتصل كالكتابة المتصلة. ب تتغير في كل موضع:\n• منفرد: ب\n• بداية: بـ\n• وسط: ـبـ\n• نهاية: ـب","hint":null,"hintAr":null,"options":["ب","بـ","ـبـ","ـب"],"correctAnswer":"ـبـ","explanation":"ـبـ is the medial (middle) form of ب. Notice the connecting lines on both sides. In بيت (house), the ب is at the start (بـ) and connects to ي in the middle.","explanationAr":"ـبـ هي الشكل الأوسط لـ ب. لاحظ خطوط الاتصال من الجانبين","grammarNote":null,"grammarNoteAr":null,"skillType":"reading","xpReward":15,"orderIndex":9},{"id":"56a7f339-2b47-4885-9db3-25da638b1d27","lessonId":"c3151c6b-b3ba-43a3-b066-b0535adb5415","type":"free_writing","difficulty":1,"question":"Write the Arabic letter that sounds like 'b' in 'book' and has ONE dot below it.","questionAr":"اكتب الحرف العربي الذي ينطق مثل 'b' وله نقطة واحدة تحته","context":"You learned this letter in exercise 2. It's the second letter of the Arabic alphabet. It starts words like بَاب (door) and بِنْت (girl).","contextAr":"تعلمت هذا الحرف في التمرين الثاني. هو الحرف الثاني في الأبجدية. يبدأ كلمات مثل باب وبنت","hint":null,"hintAr":null,"options":null,"correctAnswer":"ب","explanation":"ب (Ba) — 1 dot below, sounds like 'b'. You now know 4 letters: أ، ب، ت، ث — the first 4 letters of the Arabic alphabet!","explanationAr":"ب (الباء) — نقطة واحدة تحت، ينطق 'ب'. تعرف الآن ٤ حروف: أ، ب، ت، ث","grammarNote":null,"grammarNoteAr":null,"skillType":"writing","xpReward":20,"orderIndex":10}]
