-43a3-b066-b0535adb5415","type":"fill_blank","difficulty":1,"question":"ب has 1 dot, ت has 2 dots. How many dots does ث have? ___","questionAr":"ب لها نقطة واحدة، ت لها نقطتان. كم نقطة لـ ث؟ ___","context":"ث (Tha) sounds like 'th' in 'think'. It appears in: ثَلْج (thalj) = snow, ثَمَر (thamar) = fruit.\n\nPattern: ب (1) → ت (2) → ث (?)","contextAr":"ث (الثاء) تنطق مثل 'th' في 'think'. تظهر في: ثَلْج = snow، ثَمَر = fruit","hint":"Follow the pattern: 1, 2, ___","hintAr":"اتبع النمط: ١، ٢، ___","options":null,"correctAnswer":"3","explanation":"ث has 3 dots above. The pattern: ب (1 dot below), ت (2 dots above), ث (3 dots above). Same shape, different dots!","explanationAr":"ث لها ثلاث نقاط فوق. النمط: ب (١)، ت (٢)، ث (٣). نفس الشكل، نقاط مختلفة!","grammarNote":null,"grammarNoteAr":null,"skillType":"reading","xpReward":15,"orderIndex":6},{"id":"9fe74a8d-3c0a-468b-afef-1e6d8692e2ce","lessonId":"ddeeec6b-63bf-46cf-bc0a-15b266d084b1","type":"multiple_choice","difficulty":1,"question":"الرَّجُل (ar-rajul = the man). How do you pronounce this?","questionAr":"الرَّجُل = the man. كيف تنطق هذا؟","context":"New vocabulary: الرَّجُل (ar-rajul) = the man\n\nر (Ra) is a Sun Letter. So الـ + رجل = ar-rajul (not al-rajul).\n\nTip: The shadda on the رّ shows the doubling!","contextAr":"مفردات جديدة: الرَّجُل = the man\n\nر حرف شمسي. الـ + رجل = ar-rajul (ليس al-rajul). الشدة على الرّ تدل على التضعيف!","hint":null,"hintAr":null,"options":["al-rajul","ar-rajul","ah-rajul","as-rajul"],"correctAnswer":"ar-rajul","explanation":"الرَّجُل = ar-rajul (the man). ر is a Sun Letter, so the ل assimilates into ر. The double ر is shown by the shadda: رَّ.","explanationAr":"الرَّجُل = ar-rajul. ر حرف شمسي، فاللام تدغم في الراء. الراء المشددة تدل على التضعيف","grammarNote":null,"grammarNoteAr":null,"skillType":"reading","xpReward":10,"orderIndex":7},{"id":"b360336c-5174-434d-a79e-292d3a0e1973","lessonId":"5415ac5a-f22c-45e2-853d-f0ae58fbcc65","type":"multiple_choice","difficulty":1,"question":"Arabic text is right-to-left, but Arabic numbers are read left-to-right! How do you read ٢٥?","questionAr":"النص العربي من اليمين لليسار، لكن الأرقام من اليسار لليمين! كيف تقرأ ٢٥؟","context":null,"contextAr":null,"hint":null,"hintAr":null,"options":["52 (fifty-two)","25 (twenty-five)","7 (seven)","It depends on the dialect"],"correctAnswer":"25 (twenty-five)","explanation":"٢٥ = 25. Arabic numerals are read left-to-right. However, the Arabic WORD for 25 is 'خمسة وعشرون' = 'five and twenty' — units first!","explanationAr":"٢٥ = 25. الأرقام تُقرأ من اليسار لليمين. لكن بالكلمات: 'خمسة وعشرون' — الآحاد أولاً!","grammarNote":null,"grammarNoteAr":null,"skillType":"reading","xpReward":15,"orderIndex":3},{"id":"19463d3a-080b-47ee-acf5-1c3fe503e4ae","lessonId":"fcc364c5-9911-4ee8-8a5d-5a4f8eb3a520","type":"multiple_choice","difficulty":1,"question":"How do you read قَلَم (qalam)?","questionAr":"كيف تقرأ قَلَم (qalam)؟","context":"New vocabulary:\n• قَلَم (qalam) = pen\n\nReading guide: قَ = 'qa' (fatha), لَ = 'la' (fatha), م = 'm'\nSo: qa-la-m = qalam","contextAr":"مفردات جديدة:\n• قَلَم = pen\n\nدليل القراءة: قَ = 'qa' (فتحة)، لَ = 'la' (فتحة)، م = 'm'","hint":null,"hintAr":null,"options":["qi-lam","qa-lam","qu-lum","qal-ma"],"correctAnswer":"qa-lam","explanation":"قَلَم (qalam) = pen. قَ (qa, fatha) + لَ (la, fatha) + م (m). The two fatha marks tell you to say 'a' after each consonant.","explanationAr":"قَلَم = pen. قَ (qa) + لَ (la) + م (m). الفتحتان تقولان لك 'آ' بعد كل حرف","grammarNote":null,"grammarNoteAr":null,"skillType":"reading","xpReward":15,"orderIndex":5},{"id":"a999aea8-4524-43d4-8498-96a71ddc9e2a","lessonId":"d9a0d0af-1c1a-4552-b0a0-91d4bcd2bd20","type":"multiple_choice","difficulty":1,"question":"شُكْراً (shukran) = Thank you. What is the most common response?","questionAr":"شُكْراً = Thank you. ما أكثر رد شائع؟","context":"New vocabulary:\n• شُكْراً (shukran) = Thank you\n• عَفْواً ('afwan) = You're welcome / Pardon me\n• تَفَضَّل (tafaddal) = Please (offering something) / Go ahead\n\nشُكْراً comes from the root ش-ك-ر (gratitude). عَفْواً comes from ع-ف-و (forgiveness/pardon).","contextAr":"مفردات جديدة:\n• شُكْراً = Thank you\n• عَفْواً = You're welcome\n• تَفَضَّل = تفضل (عرض شيء)","hint":null,"hintAr":null,"options":["أهلاً","شكراً","عَفْواً","السلام عليكم"],"correctAnswer":"عَفْواً","explanation":"عَفْواً ('afwan) = You're welcome (literally 'pardon/forgiveness'). Other responses: لا شكر على واجب (no thanks needed) or بكل سرور (with pleasure).","explanationAr":"عَفْواً = You're welcome (حرفياً: العفو/المغفرة). ردود أخرى: لا شكر على واجب، بكل سرور","grammarNote":null,"grammarNoteAr":null,"skillType":"speaking","xpReward":15,"orderIndex":7},{"id":"4a293e9a-f191-420c-a5bf-95143fc55f85","lessonId":"fcc364c5-9911-4ee8-8a5d-5a4f8eb3a520","type":"multiple_choice","difficulty":1,"question":"Arabic is usually written WITHOUT vowel marks (like reading English without vowels). But when vowels ARE shown, they appear as small marks. The mark َ (a small diagonal above) is called فَتْحَة (fatha). What vowel sound does it make?","questionAr":"العربية تُكتب عادةً بدون حركات. لكن حين تُكتب الحركات تظهر كعلامات صغيرة. العلامة َ تسمى فَتْحَة. ما صوتها؟","context":"New vocabulary — The 4 main tashkeel marks:\n• َ (fatha) = 'a' sound → بَ = 'ba'\n• ُ (damma) = 'u' sound → بُ = 'bu'\n• ِ (kasra) = 'i' sound → بِ = 'bi'\n• ْ (sukun) = no vowel → بْ = 'b' (consonant only)","contextAr":"مفردات جديدة — علامات التشكيل الأربع الرئيسية:\n• َ (فتحة) = 'آ'\n• ُ (ضمة) = 'أو'\n• ِ (كسرة) = 'إي'\n• ْ (سكون) = بدون حركة","hint":null,"hintAr":null,"options":["'u' as in 'blue'","'i' as in 'feet'","'a' as in 'bat'","No vowel sound"],"correctAnswer":"'a' as in 'bat'","explanation":"فَتْحَة (fatha) makes the 'a' sound. So بَ = 'ba', كَ = 'ka', تَ = 'ta'. The word فَتْحَة itself has fatha marks!","explanationAr":"الفتحة تنطق 'آ'. فبَ = 'ba'، كَ = 'ka'، تَ = 'ta'. كلمة فَتْحَة نفسها مع فتحات!","grammarNote":null,"grammarNoteAr":null,"skillType":"reading","xpRe